  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🍪 Cookie Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a cookie shop, a cookie delivery brand or a decorated cookie business."
    },
    "intro": "A good cookie business name is fun, short and makes people hungry, whether you sell loaded cookies, boxes by post or hand-iced biscuits for parties. This **cookie business name generator** has names in seven styles, from puns and silly names to one-word brands and decorated-cookie studios, plus names built from your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good cookie business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Dough Good</strong>: a quick pun that reads well on a box.</li><li><strong>Milk Run Cookie Co.</strong>: a delivery joke for cookies sent by post.</li><li><strong>Just One More</strong>: what everyone says about cookies.</li><li><strong>Cookies Are My Cardio</strong>: funny and very Instagram.</li><li><strong>Chonk Shop</strong>: for big, thick, loaded cookies.</li><li><strong>Pistachio Cookie Lab</strong>: a modern name built around one flavour.</li><li><strong>Cut & Iced</strong>: for decorated biscuits, saying exactly what you do.</li><li><strong>The Rosy Biscuit Co.</strong>: cute, and British in using biscuit.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How cookie business names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Loaded cookie shops</strong> go big and playful: <em>Gooey Gang Cookies</em>, <em>Stuffed Cookie Society</em>.</li><li><strong>Decorated cookie makers</strong> name the craft: royal icing (the smooth icing that sets hard), piping and sprinkles. <em>Piping Bag Co.</em>, <em>Royal Icing Cookies</em>.</li><li><strong>One-word brands</strong> such as <em>Gooey</em> or <em>Stack Cookies</em> look good on packaging, but single words are more likely to be taken, so check them carefully.</li><li><strong>Cookie or biscuit?</strong> Use the word your customers search for: soft and chunky bakes are usually cookies in the UK, and decorated party ones are often iced biscuits.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>A name from a generator is a starting point, not permission to use it. Before you order the sign, the boxes or the van livery:</p><ul><li><strong>Company register.</strong> In the UK, search Companies House; you can't register a limited company with the same name as an existing one. In the US, search your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks.</strong> Search the UK trade mark register (or the USPTO in the US) for the goods and services you'll sell.</li><li><strong>Domain and handles.</strong> Check the .co.uk or .com and the Instagram and TikTok handles you'll need.</li><li><strong>Your area.</strong> Search a map app for businesses with the same or a similar name nearby.</li></ul><p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or use the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to run most of these at once. For the full process, read our guide, <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>. This is general guidance, not legal advice.</p><p>Selling food you've baked at home counts as a food business in the UK, so register with your local council at least 28 days before you start.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Making the name work for postal boxes",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Fit it on the tape.</strong> Branded tape and stickers are the cheapest packaging, so a short name wins.</li><li><strong>Think about TikTok.</strong> Cookie businesses sell on video, and a name people can say out loud is easier to share.</li></ul><p>Baking more widely? Try the <a href=\"bakery-name-generator.html\">Bakery</a>, <a href=\"cake-business-name-generator.html\">Cake Business</a> and <a href=\"dessert-business-name-generator.html\">Dessert Business</a> name generators.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_food-names.html\">food and drink business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good cookie business names?",
        "answer": "Short, fun names that make people hungry: puns like Dough Good, funny ones like Cookies Are My Cardio, or simple brands like Pistachio Cookie Lab. Decorated-cookie makers often name the craft, like Cut & Iced."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check a cookie business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name to see whether it's free as a company name, a domain and a social media handle. Before you commit, search the official registers too: in the UK, Companies House and the UK trade mark register; in the US, your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Look on a map app for businesses with the same name nearby."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should my business say cookies or biscuits?",
        "answer": "In the US a cookie is any sweet biscuit, while in the UK <em>cookie</em> usually means the big, soft, chunky kind and <em>biscuit</em> the crisp kind you dunk in tea. Most British shops selling soft or loaded bakes still call them cookies, and decorated party ones are often <em>iced biscuits</em>. Use the word your customers would type into a search."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's a good name for a decorated cookie business?",
        "answer": "Name the craft: icing, piping, sprinkles or a couture feel. Cut & Iced, Piping Bag Co. and The Sprinkle Cookie Company all tell customers you make decorated biscuits."
      }
    ]
  }
}
